## Finding and bounded BUILD path

The accepted five-minute current-source capture still fails AC-4's maximum-gap condition: 6,050 matched frames over 302.506666 seconds, 20.000523 fps mean cadence, 89.163715 ms maximum EOF gap, and 753 of 6,049 gaps above 60 ms. The sequential traced 600-frame output-flush A/B showed a modest but inconclusive difference: read gaps above 60 ms decreased from 122/599 to 107/599 and the maximum decreased from 88.425 ms to 86.679 ms with `-flush_packets 1`; both arms still had substantial long gaps. Sequential order and strace effects mean this does not prove causality or justify a production argument change.

The approved next step is a read-only 600-frame ABBA diagnostic on `/dev/video60`: default output flushing (A), `-flush_packets 1` (B), B, A. Keep all other FFmpeg arguments, mode, queue/thread settings, and reader fixed; apply identical tracing; save no frame payload; make no source change. Compare frame counts, >60 ms read and write-boundary gaps, maxima, and write durations. This is diagnostic only and cannot pass AC-4. Preserve `timestampEof` as host-monotonic time after complete raw-frame read; PTS remain V4L2 SOE, not EOF.

